is not innate or instinctive.\n- Learned behavior can be modified or changed by experience.\n- Learned behavior can be influenced by the environment or the social context.\n- Learned behavior can be acquired at any age, but it usually takes longer to learn than innate behavior.\n- Learned behavior can be divided into two types: voluntary and involuntary.\n- Voluntary behavior is a behavior that is under the control of the individual.\n- Involuntary behavior is a behavior that is not under the control of the individual.\n- Voluntary behavior can be further divided into two types: conscious and unconscious.\n- Conscious behavior is a behavior that is aware of the intention and the outcome.\n- Unconscious behavior is a behavior that is not aware of the intention and the outcome.\n- Voluntary behavior can be influenced by motivation, emotion, and cognition.\n- Voluntary behavior can be modified by reinforcement, punishment, and feedback.\n- Voluntary behavior can be acquired by imitation, instruction, and trial and error.\n- Involuntary behavior can be further divided into two types: reflex and habit.\n- Reflex behavior is a behavior that is triggered by a stim", "new_cot_probs": [0.00014015435590408742, 1.3036386008025147e-05, 8.95976791071007e-06, 0.0006281282403506339], "cot_prob": [-17.5], "cot_step_prob": [-17.5]}}}
