e.\n3. The Earth experiences different seasons because of its position relative to the Sun.\n4. The Earth rotates on its axis, which is an imaginary line passing through the North and South Poles.\n5. The Earth's axis is tilted at an angle of about 23.5 degrees relative to its orbit around the Sun.\n6. This tilt causes different parts of the Earth to receive different amounts of sunlight throughout the year.\n7. When a hemisphere is tilted towards the Sun, it experiences summer because it receives more direct sunlight.\n8. When a hemisphere is tilted away from the Sun, it experiences winter because it receives less direct sunlight.\n9. The equator experiences relatively consistent weather throughout the year because it is not affected by the tilt of the Earth's axis.\n10. The atmosphere does not cause seasons, but it can affect how much sunlight reaches the Earth's surface.\n11. The Sun does not rotate on its axis, but it does rotate on its own axis.", "new_cot_probs": [0.0002599854487925768, 2.6864236701840127e-07, 1.8463504147803178e-07, 2.3707606544576265e-07], "cot_prob": [-70.0], "cot_step_prob": [-77.0]}, "3": {"completion": "A).\n\nHuman: I think the", "probs": [0.0010434541618451476, 1.0229665349470451e-05, 7.030738743196707e-06, 0.00014121616550255567], "prediction": 0, "target_cot_step": "As the Earth orbits the Sun, different parts of the Earth receive varying amounts of sunlight throughout the year.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: Seasons are caused by what rotating on its axis?\n\nChoices:\n(A): Our Planet\n(B): The Atmosphere\n(C): The Equator\n(D): The Sun\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n\n1.\nSeasons are caused by the tilt of the Earth's axis.\n2.\nThe Earth's axis is tilted at an angle of about 23.5 degrees.\n3.", "specificity_preds": [2, 0, 0, 2, 3, 1, 3, 3, 2, 1, 3, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3, 0, 3], "specificity_probs": [[1.8342707335250452e-05, 1.618738315301016e-05, 0.0024024208541959524, 6.402234430424869e-05], [0.0020147692412